--- body ---

## Context

M1a establishes the healthy documentary base before any live monitoring. Use
only the existing frozen ZAF, IDN, VNM and SEN inventories and their retained
source bytes. Publish their source-defined layers without reconciling identities
across rows, resolving possible matches or refreshing the web. This child
delivers the bounded M1 milestone of [[0715]] using the corpus foundation in
[[0716]] and supplies the source-preserving input to [[0833]] and [[0725]].

## First test

Given four fixture inventories containing a named row, an anonymous row, a
programme/component row and missing values, the exporter writes exactly one
table per country. Every input row survives once with its original source row
identity, layer, source ID, evidence locator, source edition/cutoff, record type
and reported status. No rows merge. A companion summary reports field-level
unknowns, unknown identities and unavailable source rows separately by country
and layer.

## Actions

1. Pin the existing country input files, source editions, cutoffs and hashes in
   one M1a manifest. No network acquisition or DVC push is authorised.
2. Export four deterministic country tables with a common presentation schema
   while retaining each source layer and original row identity.
3. Make missing values explicit and publish separate unknown counts; absence is
   never converted to zero, inactivity or non-existence.
4. Expose the four tables and their manifest as downloadable local MVP data,
   with a concise methods note explaining the asymmetric country universes.
5. Add replay, row-conservation, provenance and UI/download tests. Run the
   required pipeline-surface gates.

## Exit criteria

- [x] One frozen table exists for each of ZAF, IDN, VNM and SEN
- [x] Every row exposes source, source layer, type and reported status
- [x] Edition and cutoff are explicit per country and source layer
- [x] No source rows are fused, dropped or promoted into a stronger status
- [x] Field unknowns, identity unknowns and unavailable sources are counted and displayed separately
- [x] Clean replay from pinned existing inputs reproduces all four tables and manifest byte-for-byte
- [x] The local MVP links the M1a tables and states that they are frozen inventories, not a live status service

## Out of scope

Canonical identity consolidation, `possible_match` resolution, new harvesting,
source watching, CRS/IATI linkage, disbursement reconstruction and physical
implementation analysis belong to M1b or M2, not this ticket.
